{"n": 209, "w": 1000, "h": 764, "img": "209.webp", "text": "12-112/4\n\nTROUBLESHOOTING DME 1.7 M 42\n\nNote\nAlways conform with safety and accident prevention regulations for all tests\nand work on the engine electric and electronic system.\n\nCaution!\nDangerous high tension on primary and secondary circuits of ignition.\n\nThe battery should not be disconnected whenever possible, since otherwise\nthis would cancel the faults stored In memorles of all control units.\n\nDisconnect contro! units on wire harness only with the ignition turned off.\nTest electric leads only with disconnected control unit or component plugs.\nTesting Means:\n\nWiring diagrams can be found in “General Car Electrical System - 3 Series”\nfiles.\n\nOnly use qualilied testing leads, terminals and clips.\n\nUse 88-pin test adapter set 61 4 410.\n\nMultimeter\n\nPresentation of a memory-stored fault on screen.\n\nLocation of Fault:\n‘The number of a fault refers to the pin connection on the contro! unit. A fault\ncould be on a.component, concerned electric leads or in the control unit.\n\nType of Fault:\nShorts, breaks, exceeding of ranges or implausible functions are displayed.\n\nFrequency:\n\nInformation whether or not (brief fault) a fault exists at the moment of time. Also\ndisplay of how often the fault was recognized. If the fault no longer exists, the\nnumber of times the engine had been started since the last recognition of the\nfault is displayed.\n\nRecognition During:\n\nAdditional fault information about the operating conditions during recognition\nof a fault.\n\nList of Faults:\n\nFaults stored in memories can be displayed on the tester by selecting 900\n(Fault Memory).\n\nNo faults stored In memories.\nFunction disturbed: engine operation not possible.\nTroubleshooting:\n\nRequirements:\n\n- Starting system okay (battery charged, ignition switch and slarter okay, etc.).\n- Ground connections on battery, engine and body okay.\n\n- Specified gasoline In tank.\n\n= Engine In perfect operating condition (timing, compression, etc.).\n\na) Check power supply for DME contro! unit according to wiring diagram.\nb) Measure Input signals.\n— Speed signal trom Inductive pulse sender at starting speed (see status\ncall).\n— Alr flow sensor signals (see status call).\nc) Measure output signals.\n— Activation of fuel pump relay according to wiring diagram.\n= Ignition final stage with help of ENGINE TEST test siep 10.\n— Fuel injectors - check to component test.\nd) Test fuel pressure.\nTechnical data - see component testing chapter.\nFAULT1\n900 fault memory: 1 electric fuel pump relay\nExplanation:\nThis fault Is stored when a short occurs on relay 1 (electric fuel pump) or in\ncontrol lead to DME contro! unit pin 1. This fault Is recognized only when at\nleast’one additional final stage Is faulty.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.\n\nFAULT3\n\n900 fault memory: 3 fuel Injectors cyl. 1 +3\n\nExplanation:\n\nThis fault Is stored when shorts or breaks occur on fuel Injectors for cyl. 1 +3\nor thelr power supply leads.\n\nNote: The entire fuel injector group is stopped with a short on one fuel injector\nor its power supply lead. Two cylinders remain in operation.\n\nTroubleshooting: as displayed on screen.", "words": [["12-112/4", 0.4524, 0.0292, 0.5507, 0.0531], ["TROUBLESHOOTING", 0.0299, 0.0875, 0.1429, 0.0995], ["DME", 0.1474, 0.0889, 0.1717, 0.0995], ["1.7", 0.1768, 0.0889, 0.191, 0.0995], ["M", 0.195, 0.0889, 0.2036, 0.0995], ["42", 0.2077, 0.0889, 0.2199, 0.1001], ["Note", 0.0304, 0.1214, 0.0547, 0.1326], ["Always", 0.0299, 0.1379, 0.0694, 0.1519], ["conform", 0.0735, 0.1379, 0.1165, 0.1499], ["with", 0.1206, 0.1393, 0.1418, 0.1499], ["safety", 0.1459, 0.1386, 0.1783, 0.1532], ["and", 0.1819, 0.1393, 0.2016, 0.1499], ["accident", 0.2052, 0.1393, 0.2503, 0.1505], ["prevention", 0.2548, 0.1399, 0.3121, 0.1538], ["regulations", 0.3161, 0.1393, 0.3759, 0.1538], ["for", 0.3804, 0.1399, 0.3946, 0.1512], ["all", 0.3982, 0.1399, 0.4103, 0.1505],